            <div xml:id="d892">

                <pb facs="1035" n="917" xml:id="pg917"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">662.11173 Barley/48: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Poole</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-11-03T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                                1928—noon</hi>.</date><lb/>[Received November 3—9:25
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>229. Reference my 215 dated October 23, 10 a.m. Have been confidentially informed
                    by a competent officer of the German Foreign Office that the danger of an
                    embargo seems past.</p>
                <p>Have repeated foregoing to London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Poole</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
